{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-9-23","kind":"proposition","title":"性质与证明：整数","englishTitle":"If as many odd numbers as we please be added together, and their multitude be odd, the whole will also be odd.","book":9,"number":23,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.23","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.23/","group":"prop","sourceNumber":23,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-9-23@raw-02aa053fe7084e38","contentId":"euclid-9-23","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"02aa053fe7084e38a5d4bc38a3f75b5a35e2fbeeb8aad9d94c099de70d38dee7","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-9-23.statement","euclid-9-23.construction.1","euclid-9-23.construction.2","euclid-9-23.proof.1","euclid-9-23.proof.2","euclid-9-23.conclusion","euclid-9-23.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-9-23.statement","contentId":"euclid-9-23","revisionId":"euclid-9-23@raw-02aa053fe7084e38","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"29c1acab0f44b8972957e080ee3374aee4bd8edc17a30787952215c68a514240","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If as many odd numbers as we please be added together, and their multitude be odd, the whole will also be odd."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果有我们想要的那么多奇数 加上它们的人数 就会很奇怪"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-23.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-9-23","revisionId":"euclid-9-23@raw-02aa053fe7084e38","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"1be56dd4c8b3c1184eca305efc42499c83bfe6605a38d057649d9cd73e6921df","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For let as many odd numbers as we please, AB, BC, CD, the multitude of which is odd, be added together; I say that the whole AD is also odd."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"不论我们想多奇的数字,AB,BC,CD,其中的众多是奇怪的,加在一起;我说,整个AD也是奇怪的。"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-23.construction.2","contentId":"euclid-9-23","revisionId":"euclid-9-23@raw-02aa053fe7084e38","order":2,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"baca5a570433de20d24b829d7fa3f7ae0abe188324a9d76fc66e8d62cb594e7c","citations":["euclid-7-def-7"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let the unit DE be subtracted from CD; therefore the remainder CE is even. [[VII. Def. 7](/principles/euclid-7-def-7)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"将单位 DE从CD中减去,因此其余的CE是平的。 [[VII. Def. 7](/principles/euclid-7-def-7)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-23.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-9-23","revisionId":"euclid-9-23@raw-02aa053fe7084e38","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"13936a43869fd1397c49495bc32f6573a03a5d711983833569409a1d2438a339","citations":["euclid-9-22","euclid-9-21"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But CA is also even; [[IX. 22](/principles/euclid-9-22)] therefore the whole AE is also even. [[IX. 21](/principles/euclid-9-21)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但CA也是公平的,因此,整个AE也是公平的。 [[IX. 22](/principles/euclid-9-22)] [[IX. 21](/principles/euclid-9-21)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-23.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-9-23","revisionId":"euclid-9-23@raw-02aa053fe7084e38","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"0119222bc27eba442282a4dab206fd23c234f8bb664e026c6752387d79d51a54","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And DE is an unit."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"DE是单位"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-23.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-9-23","revisionId":"euclid-9-23@raw-02aa053fe7084e38","order":5,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"ff0228211a0b4ee0a48da6e2db702f7e4354346d46e5af283af5d3c43630b6da","citations":["euclid-7-def-7"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore AD is odd. [[VII. Def. 7](/principles/euclid-7-def-7)] Q. E. D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"所以AD是奇数 证毕。 [[VII. Def. 7](/principles/euclid-7-def-7)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-23.source","contentId":"euclid-9-23","revisionId":"euclid-9-23@raw-02aa053fe7084e38","order":6,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"c385f2ed6f6e30e7ca814a643e10ce06ba409db50b1d01d8d13c6607c2836036","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.23/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.23\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-9-23:euclid-7-def-7:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-9-23","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-9-23.construction.2","euclid-9-23.conclusion"],"targetContentId":"euclid-7-def-7","type":"depends_on","prove